ref 17592186256749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186396627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186523978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186524022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1045 "Partitions of Intervals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186180381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "bfa29f8b-fff6-5ca4-9fa7-be694c7b6715" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179978 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186177537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179978 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122864" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179978 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0, 4]$. If $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, calculate $∑_(j = 1)^(n)8(y_{j} + y_{j - 1})Δy_{j}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179978 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e015992d-dc19-5c46-a968-6f970052cd44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179980 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186177549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179980 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122923" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179980 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[- 2, 6]$?\n\n1. ${-2,-1, 0, 6}$\n2. ${0, 2, 4, 6}$\n3. $-2 < 2 < 4 < 5$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179980 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0668e0bd-4637-511c-a263-1fb809d9cda4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180381 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180381 #edb/ref 1061 22785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180381 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ef5d4a8f-ff27-5806-af27-4b7ffb16f3c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180381 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180461 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180461 #edb/ref 1061 35481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180461 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "adc61151-e0b6-5426-832a-962b7f89c76e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180461 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180462 #edb/ref 1061 35489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180462 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "589bd944-74be-586b-b8aa-de1f404e6b97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180462 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180464 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180464 #edb/ref 1061 35493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180464 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "866321d3-59e7-5859-b4e4-2adecd40dfc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180464 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180465 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180465 #edb/ref 1061 35494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180465 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "58b0b85b-9601-5c14-a9f6-12ded310b31e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180465 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180675 #edb/ref 1064 "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 <      x_1<      x_2 <      \\ldots <      x_n = b\\,.\n$$\n\nFor example, given the interval $[0,6],$ one possible partition is \n\n$$\n0 < 2 < 5 < 6.\n$$\n\nWe can express this partition using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{0,2,5,6\\}.\n$$\n\nNote that this partition breaks up the interval $[0,6]$ into the union of the following subintervals:\n\n$$\n[0,2] \\cup [2,5] \\cup [5,6]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180675 #edb/ref 1065 3874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180675 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "874ce92b-031e-55f5-92e4-5883ab9f029a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180675 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180706 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we have the partition $P=\\{0,2,5,6\\}$ of the interval $[a,b]=[0,6].$ Then, we have\n\n$$\na=\\underbrace{0}_{\\large x_0}   <   \\underbrace{2}_{\\large x_1}   <  \\underbrace{5}_{\\large x_2} <  \\underbrace{6}_{\\large x_3} =b.\n$$\n\nThis partition breaks up the interval $[0,6]$ into the union of the following subintervals:\n\n$$\n[0,2] \\cup [2,5] \\cup [5,6]\n$$\n\nThe length of the $i$th subinterval, denoted $\\Delta x_i,$ is simply the difference of the endpoints: \n\n- The length of the first interval $[0,2],$ denoted $\\Delta x_1,$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{x}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =2-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The length of the second interval $[2,5],$ denoted $\\Delta x_2,$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{x}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-{x}_{1} \\\\  & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The length of the third interval $[5,6],$ denoted $\\Delta x_3,$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{x}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-{x}_{2} \\\\  & =6-5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}Δ{x}_{i} & =Δ{x}_{1}+Δ{x}_{2}+Δ{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2+3+1 \\\\  & =6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is just the length of the interval $[0, 6].$\n\n**Note:** In general, for any partition $P=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_m\\}$ of an interval $[a,b],$ the sum \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\Delta x_i\n$$\n\n is just the length of the interval $[a, b],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =Δ{x}_{1}+Δ{x}_{2}+Δ{x}_{3}+⋯+Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =b-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180706 #edb/ref 1065 5779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180706 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "714f6267-47f5-5ba8-a3e7-3b7ef319e601" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180706 #edb/ref 1067 "Sums Over Partitions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523272 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523272 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523272 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "07195f6c-4e48-5dcc-aec2-5d69c56026d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523300 #edb/ref 1080 "200" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523300 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523300 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "154c6ccd-afa9-5d6e-b30d-795512a973b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523302 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523302 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523302 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "15b01046-18e1-58bb-9aae-addee4a5482b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523385 #edb/ref 1080 "190" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523385 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523385 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3e17c7a9-6c99-5817-8972-75e58e23f040" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523387 #edb/ref 1080 "196" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523387 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592